{"id":"000W7L","title":"Chaotic Dutch Loop (chaos construction, loop, dutch whispers)","author":"Chilly","solvedCount":0,"difficulty":5,"rating":"N/A","firstSeen":"2026-11-25T17:21:11+00:00","posted":"Heute, 18:05 Uhr","rules":"My series of chaos construction puzzles using sum dots will continue soon, along with selected puzzles from my back catalogue. But first I have a new chaos puzzle involving a looped path. I think it's quite tricky, but please enjoy.\n\nThe Rules:\n\n• Chaos construction: each row, column, and region contains the digits 1–9 exactly once each. A region is an orthogonally connected collection of cells, and regions are to be determined. One region border (black line) has already been provided.\n\n• Dutch loop: draw a single loop in the grid. The loop cannot cross or touch itself, not even diagonally. The loop must move orthogonally, and visit each region exactly once. Region borders divide the loop into segments. Each individual segment forms a Dutch Whispers line, and so adjacent digits on a segment must be at least 4 apart. There must be at least two cells on each segment to form a valid line. Note - adjacent digits on different segments may or may not be at least 4 apart.\n\n• Arrows: digits in cells with arrows count the number of loop cells seen in total in all arrow directions, including the cell itself.\n\n• Circles: digits in circles count the number of loop cells contained in the region that contains the circle.\n\nChaotic Dutch Loop\nby Chilly\n\nLink for solving on Sudokupad","solutionCode":"Row 5 with a '-' for region borders, not including grid edges.","tags":["Sudoku"],"links":[{"url":"https://sudokupad.app/91nhbat1ep","kind":"sudokupad"}],"data":"","error":null,"settings":{},"link":"https://sudokupad.app/91nhbat1ep","linkKind":"sudokupad","summary":{"format":"scl","decoded":true,"rows":9,"cols":9,"cages":0,"hasSolution":true,"features":["lines","overlays","underlays"]},"attempts":0,"fetched":"2026-11-25T17:21:11+00:00"}